    "raw_text": "\nmulti-dimensional analysis:\nLet me analyze this video based on the provided frames and the text prompt.\n\nThe text prompt describes a 15-second, 1:1 square-framed short about a person in a warm living room with a vinyl record spinning on a turntable, with the subject seated at a wooden table and a laptop nearby. The scene is intended to convey a cozy, intimate moment of listening to music.\n\nNow let me examine each dimension:\n\nVisual Quality Analysis:\n- The overall visual quality is solid and coherent across the sequence. The resolution is adequate, lighting remains natural, and color grading stays warm and consistent.\n- There are no major distortions or artifacts, and transitions between shots feel smooth. A few frames show minor softness or slight noise, but these do not significantly detract from the viewing experience.\n- Overall, Visual Quality aligns with a score of 4.\n\nText-to-Video Alignment Analysis:\n- The video largely reflects the prompt elements: a person in a warm living room, a vinyl record on a turntable, a wooden table, and a laptop present in the scene.\n- The framing is predominantly horizontal rather than strictly 1:1, which is a minor deviation from the exact aspect ratio requirement. Despite this, the core components and mood match well, supporting a strong alignment score around 4.\n\nPhysical/Common-sense Consistency:\n- The scene presents plausible physical interactions: the person’s posture, hand placement near the turntable, and the way the record spins appear believable within a real-world setting.\n- There are no obvious physics violations; any subtle inconsistencies are minor and do not undermine overall realism. This supports a high but not perfect score, i.e., 4.\n\nGround-truth scores: Visual Quality 4; Text-to-Video Alignment 4; Physical Consistency 4.\n</think>\n\n(1) visual quality: 4\n(2) text-to-video alignment: 4\n(3) physical/common-sense consistency: 4\n"
